Design a circuit that converts a 4-bit binary integer input (ranging from 0 to 9) into its corresponding 4-bit Binary-Coded Decimal (BCD) output. The module maps each valid binary input directly to its BCD representation, while any binary input greater than 9 results in a default output of 1010, indicating an invalid BCD value.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] int_data,
    output reg [3:0] bcd_data
);

