description:
Design a tristate buffer with a single data input D and an active-low output enable input nOE. When nOE is low (0), the buffer outputs the value of D on Q. When nOE is high (1), the output Q is in a high-impedance state (Z), effectively disconnecting it from the circuit. This functionality allows for controlled data flow in digital circuits and enables multiple devices to share a common output line without interference.
module top_module(
	input wire D,
	input wire nOE,
	output wire Q
);

