description:
Design a circuit that decodes a Gray code input into its corresponding binary output. The module takes a width-bit Gray code input and converts it to a width-bit binary output using a combinational logic process. The most significant bit of the output directly reflects the most significant bit of the input, while the other bits are derived by performing bitwise XOR operations based on previous output bits and the current Gray code input, ensuring accurate conversion from Gray code to binary format.
module top_module(
        gin, 
        bout
);

code:
module top_module(
        gin, 
        bout
);parameter width = 6;

input  [width-1 : 0] gin;
output [width-1 : 0] bout;

reg    [width-1 : 0] breg;
integer i;
assign bout = breg;

always @(gin)
begin
    breg[width-1] = gin[width-1];
    if (width > 1)
    begin
        for (i=width-2; i >= 0; i=i-1)
            breg[i] = breg[i+1] ^ gin[i];
    end
end

endmodule

