description:
Design a delta-sigma modulator that converts a 16-bit input digital signal into a one-bit pulse-width modulation (PWM) output. On each positive edge of the clock, the modulator updates its 17-bit accumulator by adding the input signal (with its most significant bit inverted) to the current value of the accumulator. The output `dout` represents the most significant bit of the accumulator, effectively generating a PWM signal that reflects the relative magnitude of the input signal.
module top_module(
    input [15:0] din,
    input clk_i,
    output reg dout
    );

code:
module top_module(
    input [15:0] din,
    input clk_i,
    output reg dout
    );reg [16:0] PWM_accumulator;

    always @(posedge clk_i) begin
        PWM_accumulator[16:0] = PWM_accumulator[15:0] + {~din[15], din[14:0]}; 
        dout = PWM_accumulator[16];

    end

endmodule

description:
Design a simple LED indicator circuit that changes its output color based on the state of an input signal. The module includes a counter that increments on the rising edge of a clock signal, and every time the counter reaches a certain threshold (specifically, when the 25th bit goes high), it checks the state of the input signal "jd". If "jd" is high, the LEDs will light up red; if "jd" is low, the LEDs will light up green. The outputs are two separate signals driving a red and a green LED accordingly.
