description:
Implement a 4-bit Johnson counter that takes a clock and an active-low reset signal as inputs. The counter will generate a sequence of states based on the feedback of its current outputs, specifically shifting and inverting bits to produce a unique count pattern. When the reset is activated, the counter is set to zero; otherwise, it updates its state on each clock positive edge according to the defined feedback logic.
module top_module(
  input                clk,
  input                rst_n,
  output reg  [3:0]    Q
);

code:
module top_module(
  input                clk,
  input                rst_n,
  output reg  [3:0]    Q
);wire [5:0] temp;

  assign temp = {Q[3], Q[2], Q[1], Q[0], Q[3], Q[2]};

  always @(posedge clk or negedge rst_n) begin
    if (~rst_n) begin
      Q <= 4'b0000;
    end else begin
      Q <= {temp[4], temp[5], temp[3], temp[2]};
    end
  end

endmodule

